      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we start by expressing the three integers in terms of their remainders when divided by 24. Let the three integers be \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). According to the problem, we have:\n\\[ a \\equiv 10 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\\[ b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\\[ c \\equiv 12 \\pmod{24} \\]\n\nThis means that we can write:\n\\[ a = 24k + 10 \\]\n\\[ b = 24m + 4 \\]\n\\[ c = 24n + 12 \\]\nfor some integers \\(k\\), \\(m\\), and \\(n\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the sum of these three integers:\n\\[ a + b + c = (24k + 10) + (24m + 4) + (24n + 12) \\]\n\\[ a + b + c = 24(k + m + n) + 26 \\]\n\nNow, we need to determine the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24. We can rewrite the sum as:\n\\[ a + b + c = 24(k + m + n) + 26 \\]\n\nSince \\(24(k + m + n)\\) is a multiple of 24, it leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 24. Therefore, we only need to consider the remainder of 26 when divided by 24:\n\\[ 26 \\div 24 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when \\(a + b + c\\) is divided by 24 is 2. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2} \\]",
